A reply to <a href="http://avaazimages.s3.amazonaws.com/AvaazCampaignDirector.pdf">http://avaazimages.s3.amazonaws.com/AvaazCampaignDirector.pdf</a>  <br />
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:
&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">We're *really* excited that so many great people want to help the Avaaz community build the world most people everywhere want. Don't delay in completing the form -- the deadline for first round applications is February 6th! This short application form will help us get to know you. Just answer these few questions and upload your CV/resume. We can't respond to all applicants but we'll get back to you soon if you match our needs for current positions. And we'll keep your details on file as we may well need your skills soon as we continue to expand.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">What open position(s) are you applying for?</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">CAMPAIGN DIRECTOR</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Why are you interested in working with Avaaz? [200 words max]</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">I am obsessive about developing my own use of the latest techniques in online and offline organizing, and am enthusiastic about expanding my local lobbying and fundraising to mobilize vastly larger numbers of people. I have an excellent track record of impacting local issues and am ready to move into a global arena in support of a well-known and effective organization with a mission that matters. </p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Describe yourself in 50 words or less</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">My research capacities, as well as written and oral communication skills, are those of a Ph.D. and professional public speaker, conceiving and developing initiatives is my passion, and I hope to run campaigns on an increasingly wide range of national and global issues.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Please describe a professional achievement you are proud of and the role that you played: [300 words max]<span class="apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span></span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">Co-founding and directing a local intentional distributed community (and 501c3) with a commitment to social justice and culture-change allowed me to get into the habit of tracking breaking events and seizing opportunities for new initiatives. In order to move forward sustainably, I cultivated a relational web of experts in order to set strategy and create a clear message. Recently I took over and ran the administration of a struggling local organization, in the process drafting campaign emails as well as managing various teams to support the principals in building relationships with government, funders, and businesses. Public speaking and media interactions come rather easily, as my first career was in the professional theater. </p>
<p class="MsoNormal">I was asked to be the first Executive Director and created an administration for an international peace organization, refining in the process the skills necessary to shape the overall strategic priorities of the organization, taking charge of recruitment, participating in team building and management, and originating and managing special projects. At this time I am working as a teacher of aikido and offering facilitation training to develop strong teamwork skills that are effective in various environments, from the collaborative to the hierarchical. I have been focused on my local community, so my knowledge of and engagement with emerging issues needs to grow into a more global focus, but my ongoing research work and teaching regularly engages in-depth questions of political and policy choices while cultivating a martial readiness to engage issues quickly and directly. </p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Please choose one global issue mentioned in the news today, and suggest what Avaaz might do about it: [200 words max]<span class="apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span></span></strong><span class="ss-required-asterisk"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#FE6758;background:#09294E"><span style="orphans: 2;text-align:-webkit-auto;widows: 2;-webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;
-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;word-spacing:0px">*</span></span></strong></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">Depending on Avaaz's local exposure/network, international pressure may be brought to bear so that Belgrade treats Pristina as an informal equal, because it is in everyone's best interest to reduce the potential for a return to open conflict. The narrative needed, which Avaaz can supply, assuming a strong input and appropriate language from peace and freedom activitsts on the ground, is one that can further normalize relations between Kosovo and Serbia through investment in the idea of participation in and support from the global community (perhaps as opposed to Industrial/Corporatized Globalization).</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">How do you like to be managed? On a spectrum from having lots of freedom and initiative to having a manager who works very closely with you, what's your ideal? [150 words max]<span class="apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span></span></strong><span class="ss-required-asterisk"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#FE6758;background:#09294E"><span style="orphans: 2;text-align:-webkit-auto;widows: 2;-webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;
-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;word-spacing:0px">*</span></span></strong></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">I prefer to be managed closely at first, with access to all decision-makers and consistent feedback, followed by a make-or-break period of less contact to assess my effectiveness with less guidance. After that, I prefer as much freedom as is practical to project manage and coordinate with my team.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Give an example of feedback on your performance that was both tough and valuable.</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">My association with Aiki Extensions, as their Executive Director, ended when the fundraising promised to support the administration I had created was re-directed. The Board gave feedback that I had been naive to allow myself to accept an officer's assurance that the budgeted income would be secured by others. It was very difficult to hear, but my listening response and parting analysis inclined them to invite me to sit on the Board, a position I continue to hold.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><br />
<strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;
color:white;background:#09294E"><span style="orphans: 2;text-align:-webkit-auto;
widows: 2;-webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;
float:none;word-spacing:0px">What single issue would you most like to work on, and what percentage of your time would you like to dedicate to it?<span class="apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span></span></span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">I would like to work on a wide range of issues. If I were to have the opportunity to advance the cause of taking local (community) control of policy-making and resource management, both in the United States and abroad, I would feel particularly satisfied. This would involve indigenous capacity building and organizing/facilitation/co-creativity training. Having no idea what working for Avaaz is like, it would be irresponsible to hazard a guess at how I would divide my time to make all priorities come to fruition.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">When would you be available to start?</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">Soon. At least thirty days and at most three months.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size:10.5pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:white;background:#09294E">Please upload your CV/resume and paste the link below</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">http://culturesmith.com/wagn/Download_General_CV</p>

